From 8bb50809166ec7e097edcf36d750ec28c070c3ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jordi Posthumus <jordi.posthumus@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 21:02:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(copy-drafts): publish the latest proposal's slot draft
 limits before the budget reads them

Base: candidate-37's patch head 5b7cfa37f (vLLM tree af0fb152), on 0612
(#687, #619), which made sync_slot_draft_limits non-blocking. From #855,
with 0612's test reconciled and the reset bookkeeping it no longer needs
removed.

Rationale. 0612 mirrored the copy drafter's per-slot draft limits to the
host without waiting, so the adaptive budget could cap a stale wide
schedule without an event sync stall: until the copy landed, the host
kept the previous values. Under load it often had not landed. On a
three-node ring 1,209 stale reads preceded the engine's death at
min_match=8 (#852). A stale limit wider than the latest proposal makes
the budget verify rows the proposal does not have, the scheduler's -1
placeholders. With dead-row marking on (SPARK_DS41F_DSPARK_DEAD_ROWS_TAU
above 0, no batch sharder) those rows carry confidence 0 and are padding
the router skips; with it off they are routed as live rows and their
gate logits are non-finite, which trips route_partials' device assert.
A stale limit narrower than the proposal admits fewer of its drafts.
sync_slot_draft_limits now waits for the copy (small, queued before the
drafter runs) and publishes it. add_request no longer has to replay
resets over a copy that lands later, so that bookkeeping goes.

Quality implications. The verified rows always match the latest
proposal: no placeholder row is verified whatever the dead-row setting,
and a narrow stale limit no longer drops drafts. Sampling and acceptance
rules are unchanged. The host now waits each step for the limit copy,
which lands once the previous step's target forward and sampling are
done, so its preparation of the next step overlaps less with the GPU. On
the ring that reproduced #852 (the operator's measurements, #855): the
m=8 crash on 2 of 2 boots is gone; copy-probe tokens per step are
unchanged for copy and edit, tool 6.636 -> 6.905 at m=8 and 6.083 ->
6.232 at m=16; single stream 63.87 against 64.90 and 63.58 against 64.68
tok/s (-1.6% and -1.7%, CI95 2.8%). Not yet measured here: a paired
single-stream verdict, and 8 and 16 streams.

Tests. tests/v1/spec_decode/test_copy_drafts.py: the host limits wait
for a queued copy and are the staged ones; a request added while a copy
is in flight keeps its reset; the stale-wide test keeps its placeholder
and doubling checks and drops its assertion that the sync never blocks.
test_copy_drafts.py, tests/v1/core/test_copy_drafts_scheduler.py and
tests/v1/spec_decode/test_adaptive_verification.py on candidate-37's
image: 71 passed, 1 skipped (candidate-37: 69 passed, 1 skipped).

Upstream status: local, on the local patch 0612; not submitted.
